      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "PERFECT TONIGHT (1) doesn't win out of turn. Hit the board with a minor placing last time when second (22.52) at this track. Has a good record at this journey. Capable of going well again. CHEEKY ALESSIA (6) was never in contention last time after drifting back at Shepparton, but prior to that won by 1.75 lengths at Ballarat (22.47) beating Shima Lite in a Grade 5 on August 12. A forward showing wouldn't surprise. CRUISING NAT (3) turned in a plain performance last time when eighth at this track over 450m behind Bindy Blazer (26.55) in a Grade 5. The form out of the last run is proven to be strong. Can figure in the finish. ASTON CHANT (2) cannot be left out after placing as public elect last start.",
